# Accepted on purpose (issue #70, Auth0 login): every endpoint now needs an
# Auth0 access token. Production already required a bearer, the shared access
# key, which this change removes; the web and API deploy together
# (docs/decisions.md, 2026-11-18).
DELETE /items/{id} the endpoint no longer allows anonymous access and now only accepts `auth0`
GET /catalog the endpoint no longer allows anonymous access and now only accepts `auth0`
GET /courses the endpoint no longer allows anonymous access and now only accepts `auth0`
GET /courses/{id} the endpoint no longer allows anonymous access and now only accepts `auth0`
GET /courses/{id}/items the endpoint no longer allows anonymous access and now only accepts `auth0`
GET /courses/{id}/study the endpoint no longer allows anonymous access and now only accepts `auth0`
GET /dashboard the endpoint no longer allows anonymous access and now only accepts `auth0`
GET /me the endpoint no longer allows anonymous access and now only accepts `auth0`
GET /stats the endpoint no longer allows anonymous access and now only accepts `auth0`
GET /study/review the endpoint no longer allows anonymous access and now only accepts `auth0`
PATCH /courses/{id} the endpoint no longer allows anonymous access and now only accepts `auth0`
PATCH /items/{id} the endpoint no longer allows anonymous access and now only accepts `auth0`
PATCH /me the endpoint no longer allows anonymous access and now only accepts `auth0`
POST /courses the endpoint no longer allows anonymous access and now only accepts `auth0`
POST /courses/{id}/copy the endpoint no longer allows anonymous access and now only accepts `auth0`
POST /courses/{id}/import the endpoint no longer allows anonymous access and now only accepts `auth0`
POST /courses/{id}/import/rows the endpoint no longer allows anonymous access and now only accepts `auth0`
POST /courses/{id}/units/{unitId}/items the endpoint no longer allows anonymous access and now only accepts `auth0`
POST /study/answers the endpoint no longer allows anonymous access and now only accepts `auth0`
POST /study/answers/{id}/override the endpoint no longer allows anonymous access and now only accepts `auth0`
POST /study/answers/{id}/undo the endpoint no longer allows anonymous access and now only accepts `auth0`
